From: GLM-EXL3-2x-GB10 testing line <tensorfold-zig-testing@local>
Subject: glm-cuda: TF_GLM_ABSORB_MMA=1, a prompt absorb_q/expand_v as tensor-core GEMMs (Mia 1104 0041, adapted to v1.2.3)

PROVENANCE: ported from MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-DGX-Sparks-1104,
patches/engine/0041-glm-cuda-TF_GLM_ABSORB_MMA-1-a-prompt-s-absorb_q-and.patch
(Apache-2.0, (c) MiaAI Lab) against TensorFold 00e7ddd (v1.2.2), 2026-11-04,
by this line. ADAPTATION: all 17 context-drifted hunks re-anchored onto the
v1.2.2 tree (the #1577-era rework moved the contexts; the diffstat matches
the original exactly - 9 files, 247 insertions, 7 deletions); the Fingerprint
layout bumps OUR 16 -> 17 (their base was 12). glm_glue_num.cuh (the 156-line
kernel file) applies verbatim. OPT-IN: TF_GLM_ABSORB_MMA=1 - off by default
(the fp32 summation order differs from the SIMT kernels); the numerics ride
every rank fingerprint (layout 17), so ranks that disagree refuse to start.
OWNER: this line; STATUS: EXPERIMENTAL, judged by the absorb window (their
RTX PRO 6000 claim: absorb 10.7x, expand 15.8x per matmul, +8% prefill
end-to-end; sampled outputs bit-equal to SIMT). Mia original reasoning follows.

[N][K]), 128 x 128 blocks of 8 warps, K 32 a stage in three cp.async stages, one head a z. Decode windows keep the
SIMT kernels. The weights are read as stored: no transposed copy.

Measured on one RTX PRO 6000 at 2048 rows x 32 heads: absorb 1.212 -> 0.113 ms, expand 1.471 -> 0.093 ms (10.7x and
15.8x); against float64 both paths have the same rel-RMS error (the bf16 output rounding), and sampled outputs were
bit-equal to the SIMT kernels'. The fp32 summation order differs, so the flag is off by default.

The opt-in prompt numerics are a new Settings.numerics field in every rank's fingerprint (layout 13): ranks that
disagree refuse to start.

